invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_avx2.c
catches: rsa_avx2_model_test
reason: the last group writes each register it adds to one register lower
  in the window, as the groups before it do, where it must write in
  place. The last pass of carries reads the result's lanes where the last
  group leaves them in place, so it reads every lane one register too
  high and the product's top register as zeros. bin/rsa_avx2_model_test
  compares every product with rsa_mont64.c's.

--- old
    size_t shift = next < groups ? 1 : 0;
--- new
    size_t shift = 1;
